summary:
- topic: Superintendent Appointment
  text: The board unanimously approved the contract for the new superintendent, Dr.
    Angela Atkinson-Dena, who was formally welcomed and briefly addressed the community.
- topic: Kaler Elementary Schedule
  text: The board voted to postpone action on a modified end-of-year schedule for
    Kaler Elementary to allow for more parent notification and feedback.
- topic: Public Comment
  text: Public comment included criticism of the transportation department's handling
    of buses for the Memorial Day parade and concerns from Kaler parents about the
    proposed student reassignment plan splitting their neighborhood.
- topic: Staff Resignations
  text: The superintendent reported a list of eight staff resignations, including
    teachers and administrators from across the district.
- topic: Kaler Student Attendance Proposal
  text: Assistant Superintendent Johanna Prince presented the administration's proposal
    for reassigning Kaler Elementary students to the four remaining elementary schools
    for the 2026-27 school year.
- topic: Board Debate on Kaler Proposal
  text: The board debated the Kaler student attendance proposal, with some members
    expressing concern that it unfairly burdens Kaler families and splits neighborhoods,
    leading to an initial 3-3 vote defeating the motion.
- topic: Kaler Proposal Final Vote
  text: After a motion to reconsider, the board ultimately passed the Kaler student
    attendance proposal 5-1, emphasizing the need for a robust and prioritized waiver
    process for Kaler families, including transportation support.
- topic: Staff Planning Concerns
  text: Principals and staff expressed the urgent need for a decision on attendance
    zones to allow for essential school-level planning, scheduling, and staff placements
    for the upcoming school year.
